{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  components/toc.hbs — the table of contents.

  Rendered EMPTY. assets/js/toc.js scans the post's `.gh-content` for h2/h3,
  gives each one an id, and appends an `<a class="ns-toc__link">` per heading
  into every `[data-toc]` on the page. A post with fewer than two headings
  gets no TOC at all — the elements stay `hidden` and nothing appears.

  This is the design system's `.ns-toc` (ds/components/css/toc.css), the same
  outline the docs, the lesson player and the Next.js app render. Two things
  about the contract matter:

    · The links are DIRECT CHILDREN of `.ns-toc`. It is a flex column, not a
      list — putting a <ul> in between breaks the rail's leading border and
      the active item's brand bar. That is why toc.js appends to [data-toc]
      itself rather than to an inner list.
    · The active item is `aria-current="true"`, NOT a class. The CSS keys off
      the same attribute the screen reader announces, so the highlighted item
      and the announced item cannot drift apart.

  TWO INSTANCES, because a sticky rail and a phone need different objects:
  the <nav> is the rail (lg and up), the <details> is the disclosure that
  replaces it below lg. toc.js fills both.

  Params
    variant   extra .ns-toc--* on the desktop rail — `ns-toc--card` for a
              sidebar that already holds other blocks, `ns-toc--numbered` for
              a procedure where the order is the content.
    title     the rail's label. Defaults to "On this page".
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{!-- Both start hidden and are revealed by toc.js adding `.is-ready` (see
     2-components/toc.css) — NOT by toggling Tailwind's `hidden`, because each
     one also carries a responsive display of its own that `hidden` would
     fight with. --}}

{{!-- The sticky rail — lg and up --}}
<nav data-toc aria-label="{{t "Table of contents"}}"
     class="js-toc ns-toc {{variant}} max-lg:hidden">
  <span class="ns-toc__title">{{#if title}}{{title}}{{else}}{{t "On this page"}}{{/if}}</span>
  <span class="ns-toc__progress" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</nav>

{{!-- The disclosure — below lg, where a sticky rail has nowhere to stick --}}
<details data-toc class="js-toc ns-toc ns-toc--collapsible lg:hidden">
  <summary>{{> icons name="list"}}{{#if title}}{{title}}{{else}}{{t "On this page"}}{{/if}}{{> icons name="caret-down"}}</summary>
</details>
